Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mv88e6xxx: honor per-port CPU affinity in VLAN maps

Use the assigned upstream port when rebuilding a local standalone port's
VLAN map. Otherwise a bridge leave overwrites a previously selected CPU
port with the switch-wide default.

For local bridged ingress, retain the bridge members and DSA links but
include only the assigned CPU port. Flooding to every CPU port delivers
duplicate frames to the host. Similarly, exclude CPU ports from virtual
bridge PVT entries used for TX forwarding offload: these frames originate
at the host and must not be reflected through another CPU link.

Leave the existing remote physical-port PVT routing unchanged.

---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mv88e6xxx/chip.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mv88e6xxx/chip.c
@@ -1570,15 +1570,20 @@
 	/* Frames from standalone user ports can only egress on the
 	 * upstream port.
 	 */
-	if (!dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp))
+	if (!dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp)) {
+		if (dp->ds == ds)
+			return BIT(dsa_upstream_port(ds, dp->index));
+
 		return BIT(dsa_switch_upstream_port(ds));
+	}
 
-	/* Frames from bridged user ports can egress any local DSA
-	 * links and CPU ports, as well as any local member of their
-	 * bridge group.
+	/* Locally received frames must reach only the assigned CPU port.
+	 * Frames injected on behalf of a virtual bridge must not be sent
+	 * back to any CPU port. Preserve the cross-chip forwarding paths.
 	 */
 	dsa_switch_for_each_port(other_dp, ds)
-		if (other_dp->type == DSA_PORT_TYPE_CPU ||
+		if ((dsa_port_is_cpu(other_dp) && dev <= dst->last_switch &&
+		     (dp->ds != ds || other_dp == dp->cpu_dp)) ||
 		    other_dp->type == DSA_PORT_TYPE_DSA ||
 		    dsa_port_bridge_same(dp, other_dp))
 			pvlan |= BIT(other_dp->index);
